      "side": 1,
      "message": "@essick@google.com: Not completely sure if this answers your question, but: Reading go/android-flag-containers and go/mainline-trunk-stable-g3doc#mainline-flag-container, I think the flag being added in aosp/3290721 is in the wrong \u0027container\u0027.\n\nIt\u0027s currently in `container: \"system\",` (from the `android.media.playback.flags-aconfig` declaration)\n\nBut go/mainline-trunk-stable-g3doc#mainline-flag-container says:\n\n\u003e Each flag has a container. The values for a container can be system, vendor, \u003capex\u003e (e.g. com.android.\u003cmodule\u003e), among other possible values.\n\u003e\n\u003e A flag is a Mainline flag if its container is an apex. \n\nSo I guess the flag needs to be defined in the `com.android.media` container instead?",
      "parentUuid": "0aa8d783_2da108b6",
